From: Indr1d-C0ld <102763446+Indr1d-C0ld@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:26:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] SAGA2: Merge prototype immunities into loaded actors

The effective resistances and immunities of an actor are saved with the
game, and the prototype's own bits are always part of them. Merging the
prototype bits back in on load makes corrected prototype data (such as
the restoration's fix making the ghost child Rallo Jovanc immune to
damage) apply to games saved before the correction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engines/saga2/actor.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/saga2/actor.cpp b/engines/saga2/actor.cpp
index 29e5053c..99c9b8f6 100644
--- a/engines/saga2/actor.cpp
+++ b/engines/saga2/actor.cpp
@@ -1207,6 +1207,13 @@ Actor::Actor(Common::InSaveFile *in) : GameObject(in) {
 	_actionCounter = in->readByte();
 	_effectiveResistance = in->readUint16LE();
 	_effectiveImmunity = in->readUint16LE();
+	//  The prototype's own resistances and immunities are always part of the
+	//  effective ones. Merge them back in, so that corrected prototype data
+	//  also applies to games saved before the correction.
+	if (_prototype) {
+		_effectiveResistance |= getBaseResistance();
+		_effectiveImmunity |= getBaseImmunity();
+	}
 	_recPointsPerUpdate = in->readSint16LE();
 	_currentRecoveryPoints = in->readUint16LE();
 
